Description: QOpenGLWidget: show a stereo widget in a stereo window of its own
 On Wayland a QOpenGLWidget that asks for stereo made its whole top-level window
 a stereo surface. Add the platform capability StereoNativeWindows (Wayland, with
 stereo EGL surfaces): a widget that renders stereo gets a native window of its own
 with a stereo format, its siblings and ancestors stay in the one-eye top-level
 surface, and a top-level window is stereo only when its own widget renders stereo.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-07

